## Rendering vocabulary

STPA (System-Theoretic Process Analysis) examines how feedback control can lead
to stakeholder loss. In this project, an ICA is one concrete unsafe-control
finding for a fixed controller, control action, and action category.

PM-* is decision-relevant process-model information held by a controller; FB-*
is feedback that updates it; CA-* is a control action that influences a
controlled process. These references are trace keys. Their supplied
descriptions carry the meaning.

This call renders the already validated causal scenario. It must not choose a
new cause, mechanism, action, hazard, constraint, loss, or delivery route.

Taxonomy obligations are analysis provenance, not causal evidence. A pattern
name, concern, or rationale may explain why the ICA was reviewed, but it does
not prove attacker access, a mechanism, or a new causal bridge. Use only the
declared factors, exact path references, and typed capability evidence.
